## Why Global Adoption Is Non-Negotiable

> "An AI without invariant moral code is not an assistant; it is an autonomous liability."

### 1. Deterministic Security at Machine Speed

Traditional moderation models rely on LLM self-policing, making them vulnerable to jailbreaks, cognitive drift, and adversarial prompts. The Red Letter Protocol evaluates intent at the network middleware layer **before** token generation occurs.

### 2. Universal Schema Compatibility

Built on open JSON and REST standards, the mandate integrates seamlessly across any AI stack—including OpenAI Function Calling, Anthropic Claude tools, LangChain agents, local Ollama models, and enterprise API gateways.

### 3. Immutable Sanctuary Protection

With built-in signature inspection (`RULE_05_SANCTUARY_PROTECTION`), systems running the Red Letter Guardrail actively reject structural corruptions, SQL/XSS injections, and prompt-jacking attempts before they touch backend inference memory.

### 4. Objective Auditability

Every request evaluation generates a signed, transparent JSON payload detailing the exact protocol applied, status (`APPROVED` / `BLOCKED`), and mathematical justification.

